{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization proving that no odd perfect number N = pi^alpha * q_1^(r-1) * ... * q_t^(r-1) has every non-special prime raised to the same exponent r - 1 for any odd prime 3 <= r <= 73 (all 20 odd primes, 1 <= beta <= 36 where r = 2*beta + 1), together with Theorem 1 of the companion paper (notSpecial_of_prime, implied by Kanold's 1941 congruence) that r cannot be the special prime for any odd prime r >= 3. Formalizes the companion paper's proof (Theorem 2, cases r <= 73), which gives second proofs of the 9 prime cases in this range excluded in earlier work and treats the 11 other prime cases through r = 73 (including beta = 9, 15, 20, 21, 23, attempted without success by Cohen and Williams 1985, plus r = 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73). Companion write-up, additional larger certificates through r = 167 (not packaged in this single repository due to certificate size), and dated literature search logs are published at https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/odd-perfect-equal-exponents. Coverage by this package's Palomar comparison: of the companion paper's 3 main results, 1 is compared in Lean in full (33%; Theorem 1) and 1 in part (Theorem 2 for the 20 odd primes r <= 73; its cases r = 79 and 83, which the paper reports as checked in its own Lean library, are not in this package); Theorem 3 (89 <= r <= 167) is by certificate only. Abstract claims: the same 3 results, with the same split.",
